CORE
main.c
--paths lifo
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
If-conversion turns the conditional write `if(c) x = 1;` into the
unconditional `x = c ? 1 : x`, which would lose the other thread's write to x
when it happens between the read and the write of x. Hence concurrent
programs must not be converted.
